Game of Thrones night king is a  terrifying villain but he may have a  connection to one of westeros 'iz most  noble families House Stark in both the  books and TV series there are plenty of  hints indicating that the night king  could actually be a stark to understand  the connection between House Stark and  the leader of the others it's important  to understand the beginnings of each  according to the world of Ice and Fire  the long night was a winter that lasted  for an entire generation thousands of  years before the story we know takes  place during the long night the others  terrorized the first men the humans who  had settled in Westeros after much  fighting with the others one of the  first men reached an agreement with the  magical beings called the children of  the forest and joined forces with them  to repel the others who are you the fuss  man called us the children but we were  born long before them no one knows for  certain who that person was but it's  hinted that this legendary hero was bran  the Builder the first Stark who helped  establish the Nights Watch bran would go  on to work with the children to build  the magically protected wall to help  defend against the others though this  battle and the walls construction was  the first interaction between the Starks  and the others it was far from the last  before we go any further there's an  important distinction to be made between  two key figures the night King and the  night's king the night king is the  leader of the White Walkers in the game  of thrones TV series the night's king  however is someone briefly touched upon  in the Song of Ice and Fire books the  night's king was a human and the  thirteenth Lord Commander of the Nights  Watch to give you an idea of how long  ago this was Jon Snow is the 998 Lord  Commander or was briefly while serving  as commander the night's king fell in  love with a mysterious woman and  together they began making human  sacrifices to the others after 13 years  with the help of House Stark the night's  king and his otherworldly wife were both  defeated the similar names have led some  to speculate that the two may be the  same person but when asked about the  possibility george RR martin asserted  otherwise writing as for the night's  king in the books he is a legendary  figure akin to land the clever and  Brandon the Builder and no more likely  to have survived to the  day than they have so that's that  they're two different people but they  also may be deeply connected by a lot  more than just their similar names so  who is the mysterious woman who won the  heart of the old night's king turning  him to the other side it said that the  thirteenth Lord Commander saw this woman  from atop the wall in a storm of sorts  she said to have skin as white as the  moon and eyes like blue stars with skin  as cold as ice the description heavily  implies that she was one of the others  sharing their frigid pale skin and  glowing blue eyes when brand tells the  story of the night's king in a storm of  sorts he indicates that the man gave  more than just his love to the woman he  gave his soul as well  the official histories of the seven  kingdoms as represented in the world of  Ice and Fire speculate that the night's  king came from one of the northern  families of which there are many but  when old nan tells the story to bran as  bran recalls in a storm of sorts she  puts all other possibilities to rest  saying without a doubt he was a stark  the brother of the man who brought him  down the idea that the night's came from  long ago was a stark suggests that the  modern-day night king might have a  similar origin story possibly being a  stark himself when he was still a normal  men one of the most heinous taboos in  Westeros is slaying one's own kin only  in the most extreme of circumstances  which is such an act be considered  justifiable Brandon the breaker had no  problem killing his brother the night's  king but what if the night's king and  his mysterious lover had a child as old  nan confirms to bran in the novel's it's  entirely possible with human white  Walker couplings resulting in what she  calls quote terrible half-human children  slaying the night's king is one thing  but an innocent offspring that seems  like a line that a stark wouldn't cross  and supposing further that brand spared  this child's life and then raised them  as a stark it could mean that the  night's Kings coupling with in other  introduced the blood of the others into  the stark line from very early on in the  family's history if that theory is true  the family's affinity for the cold feels  pretty natural as Catelyn Stark put it  in the books  the Starks were made for the cold  the seventh season finale the dragon and  the wolf ends on an ominous note as the  White Walkers break through the wall and  march into Westeros during the scene the  camera shows a bird's-eye view of the  army of the Dead marching forward what's  interesting about this shot is that the  White Walkers march in a formation that  appears highly reminiscent of the Starks  house sigil the image is flipped but the  resemblance is uncanny  there's clearly some sort of connection  between the stark house and the White  Walkers and by extension the knight King  a common theme in A Song of Ice and Fire  is the burden placed on characters by  their ancestors  Tyrion tries to prove his worth to his  father but ultimately has to come to  terms with his disapproval Jon Snow  grows up thinking he's illegitimate  denied the knowledge that he's heir to  the Iron Throne and Daenerys lives in  the shadow of her father the Mad King  Aerys ii and his terrible actions which  led to the near destruction of the  Targaryen house I'm not my father  no your eyes thank the gods if the  thirteenth Lord Commander of the Nights  Watch was a stark who fell in love with  one of the others it's not a stretch to  imagine that the other members of the  family could have crossed over to their  side as well we know from the show that  the night king used to be a man and  considering the history it makes the  most sense that the night king was a  stark if it's true it'll be a real cold  reckoning for the surviving members of  House Stark it would be especially  stressful for Jon Snow it's one thing to  find out he's related to his girlfriend  but his mortal enemy - it's almost too  much to keep track of that's why I read  so much Jon Snow check out one of our  newest videos right here plus even more  looper videos about your favorite stuff  are coming soon subscribe to our YouTube  channel and hit the bell so you don't  miss a single one  [Music]
 

